# refund-api local environment (direnv).
#
# T4 (this bootstrap) needs no 1Password-sourced secrets: every var required
# so far (DATABASE_URL, ALLOWED_ORIGINS, AUTH_JWKS_URL, AUTH_ISSUER,
# AUTH_AUDIENCE, PORT, NODE_ENV — see .env.example) is a non-secret local
# default shared across every developer's machine, identical in spirit to
# estimai-api/notify-api today (neither has committed a .envrc either, for the
# same reason — they load a plain, gitignored `.env` copied from
# .env.example). This file exists now so the wiring point is in place: once
# T9 (REFUND_S3_*) and T13/T19 (NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN) add real secrets, this
# should become a 1Password-backed cache file, following auth/.envrc's exact
# pattern: guard on a gitignored `.env.cached`, populate it with one `op read`
# per secret against the real vault item (create it in 1Password first — do
# not invent placeholder vault paths here), then `source .env.cached`.
#
# Until then, direnv simply loads the local, gitignored .env (see .env.example
# for the template — copy it to .env and fill in values, same as every other
# Operai backend).
dotenv_if_exists .env
